WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.035 --> 00:00:03.036
-As he faces
only the third

00:00:03.036 --> 00:00:04.770
Senate impeachment trial
in history,

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:07.273
the president is desperately
trying soothe his ego

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:09.642
and pretend he doesn't know
the key players in the scandal.

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:11.711
For more on this, it's time for
"A Closer Look."

00:00:15.915 --> 00:00:17.883
In the last week,
the impeachment trial

00:00:17.883 --> 00:00:19.486
against President Trump
has been rocked

00:00:19.486 --> 00:00:21.387
by a series of
bombshell revelations

00:00:21.387 --> 00:00:23.990
from one of Trump's key henchmen
in the Ukraine scandal,

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:25.758
Lev Parnas.
Remember him?

00:00:25.758 --> 00:00:29.695
The guy who looks like a pinata,
but for crimes?

00:00:29.695 --> 00:00:31.463
The guy who looks like
a Soviet version

00:00:31.463 --> 00:00:33.132
of the sad-face emoji?

00:00:33.132 --> 00:00:34.133
[ Laughter ]

00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:35.234
A man who know, no joke,

00:00:35.234 --> 00:00:36.936
had a company called
"Fraud Guarantee."

00:00:36.936 --> 00:00:38.304
And based on how
things have gone,

00:00:38.304 --> 00:00:41.307
it turns out
he's a man of his word.

00:00:41.307 --> 00:00:43.042
The revelations began
with new evidence

00:00:43.042 --> 00:00:45.478
released by the House
that included Parnas'

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:47.413
handwritten notes
about Trump's scheme

00:00:47.413 --> 00:00:49.749
to force Ukraine to dig up dirt
on Joe Biden.

00:00:49.749 --> 00:00:51.584
The notes made it
incredibly obvious --

00:00:51.584 --> 00:00:53.486
in case there was
any doubt before --

00:00:53.486 --> 00:00:56.055
that Parnas was at the center
of a corrupt plot

00:00:56.055 --> 00:00:58.958
designed exclusively for
political and financial reasons,

00:00:58.958 --> 00:01:01.627
and involving several
of Trump's closest allies.

00:01:01.627 --> 00:01:03.496
The notes include
incriminating phrases like

00:01:03.496 --> 00:01:04.864
"Get Zelensky
to announce that

00:01:04.864 --> 00:01:06.632
the Biden case will be
investigated,"

00:01:06.632 --> 00:01:09.234
"do my magic and cut deal,"
"get deal done,"

00:01:09.234 --> 00:01:10.536
"one to three months,"

00:01:10.536 --> 00:01:13.606
and the ambiguous phrase
"Ukraine ledger."

00:01:13.606 --> 00:01:16.376
The only way these notes
could be any more suspicious

00:01:16.376 --> 00:01:18.745
is if the letters
were cut out from magazines.

00:01:18.745 --> 00:01:20.079
[ Laughter ]

00:01:20.079 --> 00:01:22.681
These notes looked like clues
James Bond would find

00:01:22.681 --> 00:01:25.351
in an underground lair
right before he turns around,

00:01:25.351 --> 00:01:27.620
and sees Christoph Waltz
dangling Joe Biden

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:29.489
above a shark tank.

00:01:29.489 --> 00:01:34.194
"Ah, James, you're probably
here to rescue your old chum."

00:01:36.529 --> 00:01:40.166
And then, after all of those
notes, there was one other note

00:01:40.166 --> 00:01:41.701
that referred to Trump's
personal lawyer,

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:44.203
Rudy Giuliani -- the man at the
center of this entire scheme --

00:01:44.203 --> 00:01:46.538
with just the word "Rudy"
and two asterisks.

00:01:46.538 --> 00:01:48.240
These guys are so dumb

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:51.211
they literally wrote down the
names of their co-conspirators.

00:01:51.211 --> 00:01:53.880
This is like if Al Cowlings
had put a sticker

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:55.815
on the inside of his white
Ford Bronco

00:01:55.815 --> 00:01:57.317
that said "OJ on board."

00:01:57.317 --> 00:01:59.085
[ Laughter ]

00:01:59.085 --> 00:02:01.654
And yet, as incriminating
as these notes would seem,

00:02:01.654 --> 00:02:04.424
Trump supporters have gone to
extreme lengths to dismiss them.

00:02:04.424 --> 00:02:06.959
For instance, Fox host
Laura Ingraham said

00:02:06.959 --> 00:02:08.227
they were meaningless.

00:02:08.227 --> 00:02:10.262
-We got these notes of,
like, scribble scrabble

00:02:10.262 --> 00:02:12.298
on a Ritz-Carlton
Vienna notepad,

00:02:12.298 --> 00:02:13.399
and we're supposed
to all think,

00:02:13.399 --> 00:02:16.035
"Oh, the Democrats
have a smoking gun."

00:02:16.035 --> 00:02:17.636
-First of all,
you're accusing someone else

00:02:17.636 --> 00:02:18.805
of scribble scrabble?

00:02:18.805 --> 00:02:20.373
Donald Trump can't even sign
his own name.

00:02:20.373 --> 00:02:23.809
If you didn't know, that is
the president's signature.

00:02:23.809 --> 00:02:25.111
If you looked at it
for the first time,

00:02:25.111 --> 00:02:26.478
you'd be like, "I guess that's
a prescription for,

00:02:26.478 --> 00:02:27.780
I don't know,
Percocet?"

00:02:29.181 --> 00:02:31.984
Second, these are notes on a
Ritz-Carlton Vienna notepad.

00:02:31.984 --> 00:02:34.186
The Ritz-Carlton Vienna
sounds like the setting

00:02:34.186 --> 00:02:36.355
for literally every spy movie
ever made.

00:02:36.355 --> 00:02:40.960
They probably have tranquillizer
darts in the mini bar.

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:42.862
Without looking it up,
I can say for certain

00:02:42.862 --> 00:02:44.931
there's at least one
"Mission: Impossible" movie

00:02:44.931 --> 00:02:46.832
where Tom Cruise parachutes
out of an airplane,

00:02:46.832 --> 00:02:48.968
and crashes through the windows
of the Ritz-Carlton Vienna.

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:51.437
Except, in this sequel,
he crashed through the window

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:53.272
in the first five minutes,
and found a note that said,

00:02:53.272 --> 00:02:54.640
"Here's our plan,
and how to stop us.

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:55.775
The movie is over now."

00:02:55.775 --> 00:02:57.143
[ Laughter ]

00:02:57.143 --> 00:02:59.879
Then, of course, there was
Parnas' bombshell interview

00:02:59.879 --> 00:03:01.714
with Rachel Maddow,
where he confirmed

00:03:01.714 --> 00:03:04.817
all sorts of sordid details,
including the fact that Trump

00:03:04.817 --> 00:03:07.419
was willing to withhold
all aid to Ukraine

00:03:07.419 --> 00:03:09.088
unless they
specifically promised

00:03:09.088 --> 00:03:10.623
to dig up dirt
on Biden.

00:03:10.623 --> 00:03:12.958
Yet still,
Trump allies in the Senate

00:03:12.958 --> 00:03:15.061
have basically decided to
pretend it didn't happen --

00:03:15.061 --> 00:03:18.163
like Martha McSally,
who made a big show of attacking

00:03:18.163 --> 00:03:21.601
CNN reporter Manu Raju simply
for asking if she thought

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:23.436
the new evidence
offered by Parnas

00:03:23.436 --> 00:03:24.837
should be included
in the trial.

00:03:24.837 --> 00:03:27.273
-Senator McSally, should the
Senate consider new evidence

00:03:27.273 --> 00:03:28.975
as part of
the impeachment trial?

00:03:28.975 --> 00:03:31.410
-Manu, you're a liberal hack.
I'm not talking to you.

00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:33.779
-You're not gonna comment?
-You're a liberal hack.

00:03:33.779 --> 00:03:34.780
-She might as well
have said,

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:38.017
"I'd like to speak
to your manager."

00:03:38.017 --> 00:03:40.420
This one moment shows
just how deeply and fully

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:43.156
the Republican party has become
the party of Donald Trump.

00:03:43.156 --> 00:03:45.057
All that reporter did
was ask a simple,

00:03:45.057 --> 00:03:47.427
straightforward question,
and she accused him of bias.

00:03:47.427 --> 00:03:49.729
I feel like this isn't
the first time

00:03:49.729 --> 00:03:51.197
she's reacted
like that, either.

00:03:51.197 --> 00:03:52.765
"You know what?
You're a hack."

00:03:52.765 --> 00:03:55.735
"Okay, ma'am, but you still
have to pay for extra guac."

00:03:55.735 --> 00:03:57.904
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.904 --> 00:03:59.972
And then, of course,
there's Trump himself,

00:03:59.972 --> 00:04:02.642
who denied ever knowing Parnas
despite the fact that

00:04:02.642 --> 00:04:05.478
Trump has had at least 10
separate interactions with him,

00:04:05.478 --> 00:04:07.579
and has been in multiple
photos with him --

00:04:07.579 --> 00:04:09.382
a fact Trump brushed off.

00:04:09.382 --> 00:04:11.250
-What is your response
to Lev Parnas,

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:15.154
who said that your efforts in
Ukraine were all about 2020?

00:04:15.154 --> 00:04:17.356
You just wanted
Joe Biden out.

00:04:17.356 --> 00:04:18.424
-Well, I don't know him.

00:04:18.424 --> 00:04:19.892
I don't know Parnas,
other than,

00:04:19.892 --> 00:04:21.627
I guess I had
pictures taken --

00:04:21.627 --> 00:04:23.095
which do I with thousands
of people.

00:04:23.095 --> 00:04:25.798
He's trying to probably
make a deal for himself.

00:04:26.899 --> 00:04:28.734
I don't even who
know this man is,

00:04:28.734 --> 00:04:31.037
other than, I guess
he attended fundraisers,

00:04:31.037 --> 00:04:33.072
so I take a picture
with him.

00:04:33.072 --> 00:04:35.141
I'm in a room.
I take pictures with people.

00:04:35.141 --> 00:04:38.410
I take thousands and thousands
of pictures with people

00:04:38.410 --> 00:04:39.478
all the time --

00:04:39.478 --> 00:04:41.413
thousands during course
of a year.

00:04:41.413 --> 00:04:43.749
-Okay, it's true that you
have photos with lots of people,

00:04:43.749 --> 00:04:45.551
but you also have photos
with lots of criminals.

00:04:45.551 --> 00:04:46.886
You have photos
with Michael Cohen,

00:04:46.886 --> 00:04:48.487
who's now in jail,
and Paul Manafort,

00:04:48.487 --> 00:04:50.322
who's now in jail,
and Kid Rock,

00:04:50.322 --> 00:04:52.258
who, at the very least,
should be in fashion jail

00:04:52.258 --> 00:04:54.727
for those
American-flag pants.

00:04:54.727 --> 00:04:56.362
Trump is lying
because he knows

00:04:56.362 --> 00:04:58.297
that he's only the third
president in history

00:04:58.297 --> 00:05:00.800
to face a Senate
impeachment trial.

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:02.334
His name and presidency

00:05:02.334 --> 00:05:04.637
will be stained in
the history books forever,

00:05:04.637 --> 00:05:07.039
regardless of what happens --
which is pretty remarkable

00:05:07.039 --> 00:05:09.608
given that, just a few years
ago, he was mostly known as

00:05:09.608 --> 00:05:11.511
the "you're fired" guy.

00:05:11.511 --> 00:05:14.346
This is like if the "can you
hear me now" guy got arrested

00:05:14.346 --> 00:05:17.617
for burning down
a Verizon store.

00:05:17.617 --> 00:05:21.086
You'd realize, "Oh, now I know
why he switched to Sprint."

00:05:21.887 --> 00:05:25.024
No matter how hard Republicans
try to rig the Senate trial

00:05:25.024 --> 00:05:27.960
to let Trump off easy,
the mark of this historic moment

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:29.328
will never go away.

00:05:29.328 --> 00:05:31.230
And that's something Trump
is very obviously aware of,

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:33.365
because last week,
as the House voted

00:05:33.365 --> 00:05:35.901
to officially transmit
the articles of impeachment

00:05:35.901 --> 00:05:38.638
they had passed in December
to the Senate for a trial,

00:05:38.638 --> 00:05:40.139
Trump freaked out
on Twitter.

00:05:40.139 --> 00:05:42.441
-He asked "Why should I have
the stigma of impeachment

00:05:42.441 --> 00:05:45.511
attached to my name
when I did nothing wrong?"

00:05:45.511 --> 00:05:48.047
-In all caps,
he tweeted, quote,

00:05:48.047 --> 00:05:52.318
"I just got impeached for making
a perfect phone call."

00:05:52.318 --> 00:05:54.086
-I mean,
I wouldn't worry too much

00:05:54.086 --> 00:05:55.754
about the stigma
of impeachemnt,

00:05:55.754 --> 00:05:58.123
because you have so many
other stigmas.

00:05:58.123 --> 00:05:59.892
I mean, sure,

00:05:59.892 --> 00:06:01.894
you're only the third president
to get impeached,

00:06:01.894 --> 00:06:03.962
but you're the first one
to bail on an umbrella,

00:06:03.962 --> 00:06:05.631
and just leave it
outside an airplane.

00:06:05.631 --> 00:06:08.200
[ Laughter ]

00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:11.770
I'm gonna remember that more
than the impeachment thing.

00:06:11.770 --> 00:06:14.440
Second, nothing says
"perfect phone call"

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:16.608
like shouting at
the top of your lungs.

00:06:16.608 --> 00:06:19.044
If you're someone who tweets
in all caps,

00:06:19.044 --> 00:06:20.746
you're not making
perfect phone calls.

00:06:20.746 --> 00:06:24.149
Besides, we all know
the only perfect phone call

00:06:24.149 --> 00:06:28.254
is when someone calls you up
to cancel dinner plans.

00:06:28.254 --> 00:06:30.656
"Oh, my God. We don't have to
leave the house."

00:06:34.060 --> 00:06:36.963
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:42.301
"That was [bleep] perfect."

00:06:42.301 --> 00:06:43.669
[ Laughter ]

00:06:43.669 --> 00:06:45.838
And apparently, Trump's rage
isn't confined to Twitter.

00:06:45.838 --> 00:06:48.007
CNN reported over the weekend
that Trump has been

00:06:48.007 --> 00:06:50.643
shuffling around his chintzy
resort in Palm Beach,

00:06:50.643 --> 00:06:53.078
grousing to club members
about how unfair it is

00:06:53.078 --> 00:06:54.680
that he's facing
an impeachment trial.

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:55.914
-A source
close to the White House

00:06:55.914 --> 00:06:58.316
saying president Trump
has appeared distracted

00:06:58.316 --> 00:06:59.719
by the impeachment trial,

00:06:59.719 --> 00:07:01.387
telling people around him
at Mar-a-Logo

00:07:01.387 --> 00:07:04.389
he can't understand
why he was impeached.

00:07:04.389 --> 00:07:08.293
-He is a bit distracted by
the ongoing impeachment saga.

00:07:08.293 --> 00:07:10.563
He is apparently
asking people around him,

00:07:10.563 --> 00:07:12.765
"Why are they
doing this to me?"

00:07:12.765 --> 00:07:15.234
-Donald Trump not knowing
why he is impeached

00:07:15.234 --> 00:07:17.703
is in itself
an impeachable offense.

00:07:17.703 --> 00:07:19.572
[ As Trump ] "Why are they
doing this to me?"

00:07:19.572 --> 00:07:22.107
[ Normal voice ]
"Well, here's a 300-page
document laying it out."

00:07:22.107 --> 00:07:23.542
[ As Trump ] "What? No.
I don't want to read that.

00:07:23.542 --> 00:07:26.078
Why?

00:07:26.078 --> 00:07:28.080
Why won't they tell me?"

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:29.948
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:31.016 --> 00:07:34.319
[ Normal voice ] Senate
Republicans are obviously intent

00:07:34.319 --> 00:07:36.421
on rigging the trial
as much as they can,

00:07:36.421 --> 00:07:38.690
but no matter what they do,
the trial itself

00:07:38.690 --> 00:07:40.993
is a significant, historic
judgment on its own,

00:07:40.993 --> 00:07:44.062
because in our current
manic news environment,

00:07:44.062 --> 00:07:45.731
everyone's memories
are fried,

00:07:45.731 --> 00:07:47.466
and nothing ever really
seems to stick.

00:07:47.466 --> 00:07:49.235
Remember when Trump tried to
fire Robert Mueller?

00:07:49.235 --> 00:07:52.238
Or when his administration made
up a fake terrorist incident

00:07:52.238 --> 00:07:53.539
called the
"Bowling Green Massacre?"

00:07:53.539 --> 00:07:56.608
Or when Trump literally shoved
a fellow NATO leader

00:07:56.608 --> 00:07:59.311
out of the way so he could get
to the front of the group?

00:07:59.311 --> 00:08:00.513
I mean, look at him.

00:08:00.513 --> 00:08:02.748
It's like he heard
there was free food

00:08:02.748 --> 00:08:03.950
in the conference room.

00:08:03.950 --> 00:08:05.250
[ Laughter ]

00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:07.586
He looks like he's at a wedding,
trying catch the bouquet.

00:08:07.586 --> 00:08:09.722
[ As Trump ]
"Go away, Melissa.

00:08:09.722 --> 00:08:12.825
You've already been
married twice."

00:08:12.825 --> 00:08:15.227
[ Normal voice ] So, knowing
that this historic mark of shame

00:08:15.227 --> 00:08:17.696
will follow him in the
history books forever,

00:08:17.696 --> 00:08:20.533
Trump's been in desperate search
of ways to soothe his ego --

00:08:20.533 --> 00:08:23.602
so desperate that, at an event
in the Oval Office last week

00:08:23.602 --> 00:08:26.238
that was meant to promote
prayer in public schools,

00:08:26.238 --> 00:08:28.340
in front of him,
on the Resolute desk,

00:08:28.340 --> 00:08:30.743
was a map that appeared
to divide the country

00:08:30.743 --> 00:08:34.279
into a red-blue map based on
the 2016 election results.

00:08:34.279 --> 00:08:37.182
Basically, they gave him
that map the way parents

00:08:37.182 --> 00:08:40.186
give their kids a maze
and crayons at a restaurant.

00:08:40.186 --> 00:08:41.787
They actually should
give him a maze,

00:08:41.787 --> 00:08:43.723
but one where
he learns something.

00:08:43.723 --> 00:08:46.458
[ Laughter ]

00:08:46.458 --> 00:08:51.029
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:51.029 --> 00:08:53.132
The weirdest part
of this charade

00:08:53.132 --> 00:08:56.301
was the fact the map
just sat there on the desk,

00:08:56.301 --> 00:08:58.670
unmentioned,
for the entire event.

00:08:58.670 --> 00:09:00.306
Trump never
talked about it.

00:09:00.306 --> 00:09:04.676
It was just there to entertain
him, and make him feel better.

00:09:04.676 --> 00:09:07.713
They might as well just have it
printed onto a blanket,

00:09:07.713 --> 00:09:09.949
so he can carry it around
Linus-style.

00:09:09.949 --> 00:09:11.850
[ Laughter ]

00:09:11.850 --> 00:09:14.019
Not only was the map
weirdly conspicuous

00:09:14.019 --> 00:09:15.955
for an event that had nothing
to do with the election,

00:09:15.955 --> 00:09:17.589
apparently,
it wasn't even correct.

00:09:17.589 --> 00:09:19.658
While it appeared
to be very red,

00:09:19.658 --> 00:09:22.261
an emotionally reassuring symbol
of his popularity,

00:09:22.261 --> 00:09:23.962
Twitter sleuths
quickly determined

00:09:23.962 --> 00:09:25.431
it wasn't
entirely accurate.

00:09:25.431 --> 00:09:27.633
Some counties
that went for Hillary Clinton

00:09:27.633 --> 00:09:28.867
were colored red.

00:09:28.867 --> 00:09:30.969
Trump's literally just changing
the electoral map

00:09:30.969 --> 00:09:32.438
to make himself
feel better now.

00:09:32.438 --> 00:09:34.773
Why not go all the way, and
include the rest of the world?

00:09:34.773 --> 00:09:37.576
[ As Trump ] "Look, everyone,
I also won Greenland, Turkey,

00:09:37.576 --> 00:09:41.580
and the Caspian Sea."

00:09:41.580 --> 00:09:43.916
Thank you, Caspia.

00:09:43.916 --> 00:09:45.985
Thank you,
Caspian people."

00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:51.456
[ Normal voice ]
So, Trump faked an electoral map
to make himself feel better,

00:09:51.456 --> 00:09:53.158
and then conspicuously
laid it out

00:09:53.158 --> 00:09:54.426
on the famous
Resolute desk,

00:09:54.426 --> 00:09:56.362
hoping people would notice it.
That is insane.

00:09:56.362 --> 00:09:59.231
It's like if you went over
to Steven Seagal's house,

00:09:59.231 --> 00:10:00.832
and he had a shelf
full of Oscars,

00:10:00.832 --> 00:10:05.037
except they were just a bunch
of Ken dolls painted gold.

00:10:05.037 --> 00:10:06.305
"I won this one for

00:10:06.305 --> 00:10:09.408
'Submarine Justice 2:
Operation Killer Seals.'"

00:10:12.278 --> 00:10:16.882
It's where I delivered
the famous line, "Hyah!"

00:10:16.882 --> 00:10:20.585
Trump knows that, ultimately,
in the eyes of history,

00:10:20.585 --> 00:10:23.389
it won't matter whether
Republicans successfully rigged

00:10:23.389 --> 00:10:25.157
his impeachment trial
to let him off the hook.

00:10:25.157 --> 00:10:27.993
No matter what, he will be only
the third President in history

00:10:27.993 --> 00:10:30.028
to face such a trial,
and it follows him forever --

00:10:30.028 --> 00:10:32.631
especially as more damning
evidence emerges.

00:10:32.631 --> 00:10:35.233
A few years from now,
when they're asked about

00:10:35.233 --> 00:10:37.235
where they stood on the
presidency of Donald Trump,

00:10:37.235 --> 00:10:39.338
I have a feeling a lot of
Republicans will say...

00:10:39.338 --> 00:10:40.473
-I don't know him.

00:10:40.473 --> 00:10:42.675
-This has been
"A Closer Look."

